---
description: ZeroData Chat architecture invariants for agents
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow `.agent/rules.md` as the source of truth.

- UI is Jetpack Compose; ViewModels expose StateFlow; chat I/O goes through `ChatRepository` only.
- Never call `MqttManager` or `AppDatabase` from UI or ViewModels for chat flows.
- Personal chats use `ChatUtils.getCanonicalChatId(user1, user2)` (sorted ids joined by `_`). Never mint random 1:1 chat IDs.
- Room entities stay inside the repository; map to `Chat` / `Message` before ViewModels.
- MQTT topics live in `Constants.kt`. Payload format is JSON via `MqttPayloadMapper`.
- Do not remove `GlobalExceptionHandler` or change `CrashActivity` unless the user asks.
- Dark Material3 theme (`0xFF121212`). The Add-chat dialog is a required hub action.
